                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fc26fad8-cc5a-4674-9ee7-5540e51891c7",
                        "source_entry_id": "e69263ec-200e-321c-b564-efd3275f652b",
                        "source_sense_description": "3. Homme méprisable",
                        "target_lang_word": "cur",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cur",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f456aaab-9e66-3b15-be61-2abe9e6a36c6",
                                        "entry_id": "853e333d-f80a-321a-9f19-ee0bfe8ceabd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A contemptible or inferior dog."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated",
                                            "humorous"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1627a352-3ea8-40c0-861d-a327919022af",
                                                "sense_id": "f456aaab-9e66-3b15-be61-2abe9e6a36c6",
                                                "text": "A fals double tunge is more fiers and fell\nThen Cerberus the cur couching in the kenel of hel;\nWherof hereafter, I thinke for to write,"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "23a187af-6e9a-490f-a6a2-fe02a51104d2",
                                                "sense_id": "f456aaab-9e66-3b15-be61-2abe9e6a36c6",
                                                "text": "you have many enemies, that know not why they are so, but, like to village-curs, bark when their fellows do."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "871bec4f-daaa-4ac1-9984-31efbc7c915a",
                                                "sense_id": "f456aaab-9e66-3b15-be61-2abe9e6a36c6",
                                                "text": "A Churliſh Envious Curr vvas gotten into a Manger, and there lay Growling and Snarling to keep the Horſes from their Provender. The Dog Eat None himſelf, and yet rather Ventur'd the Starving his Own Carcaſe then he would ſuffer any thing elfe to be the Better for't."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b219a2cc-84a5-467a-be4e-8fd9fbb24c14",
                                                "sense_id": "f456aaab-9e66-3b15-be61-2abe9e6a36c6",
                                                "text": "He threw the soapsuds skilfully over a wretched little yellow cur he had, then turning his face to the agent's house, he shouted from the distance, \"All the men gone last night!\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b54401a1-5bea-4853-810a-04865a800e92",
                                                "sense_id": "f456aaab-9e66-3b15-be61-2abe9e6a36c6",
                                                "text": "\"You have no more spirit than a mongrel cur. You lie down on the ground and ask people to trample on you.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4696ee56-7c28-3337-83e1-c6cb811dc9f2",
                                        "entry_id": "853e333d-f80a-321a-9f19-ee0bfe8ceabd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A detestable person."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated",
                                            "humorous"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9210cac8-9ee4-499e-bc7b-1b9419abb2dc",
                                                "sense_id": "4696ee56-7c28-3337-83e1-c6cb811dc9f2",
                                                "text": "This butcher's cur is venom-mouth'd, and I have not the power to muzzle him."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ae1f8b5b-113f-4695-99f5-f084ed38a109",
                                                "sense_id": "4696ee56-7c28-3337-83e1-c6cb811dc9f2",
                                                "text": "\"Who 's a cur - now - hey?\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1ba05934-d98b-4f53-9fd4-00a5269ff6c4",
                                                "sense_id": "4696ee56-7c28-3337-83e1-c6cb811dc9f2",
                                                "text": "Clayton interrupted him. “Stop!” he cried. “Stop! What manner of cur are you that you traduce the character of a good woman whom we believe dead! God!”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2e3814bd-db84-30f5-80b9-76548bae868e",
                                        "entry_id": "853e333d-f80a-321a-9f19-ee0bfe8ceabd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A sheepdog or watchdog."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "dialectal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7fff97f7-d2fe-4645-8743-8f4214e33bd9",
                                                "sense_id": "2e3814bd-db84-30f5-80b9-76548bae868e",
                                                "text": "Then send our Curs to gather up the Sheep"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "552f6622-fea0-4394-9ac3-a71fe82a9b57",
                                                "sense_id": "2e3814bd-db84-30f5-80b9-76548bae868e",
                                                "text": "\"He's a good sharp cur,\" or \"a good cur,\" is said of any dog that barks at strangers and guards his master's property."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b7ed9b82-fa6c-4214-ba8f-45a217f42d6e",
                        "source_entry_id": "e69263ec-200e-321c-b564-efd3275f652b",
                        "source_sense_description": "3. Homme méprisable",
                        "target_lang_word": "keffer",
                        "target_lang_code": "nl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "keffer",
                                "target_lang_code": "nl",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dc903b6a-16c9-30a0-bcb1-35b5520b01e8",
                                        "entry_id": "18dc3669-3a95-3c2b-ab59-da3e497ba5d3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "klein hondje dat hinderlijk veel blaft"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4c10df81-8c84-4896-ab90-9fb4385d1898",
                                                "sense_id": "dc903b6a-16c9-30a0-bcb1-35b5520b01e8",
                                                "text": "Hond en ik vervolgden onze weg. Twee keer kwamen we collega’s tegen. De eerste keer twee boxers waar mijn keffer geweldig tegen tekeer ging, daarna een labrador die het ook woest moest ontgelden. Om onduidelijke redenen denkt onze hond dat zij de baas is in de buurt. Geen scooter, krantenbezorger, kat of andere hond kan passeren zonder dat zij begint te blaffen."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2135c41b-a9fb-3d89-a5d5-c57d08fef1b3",
                                        "entry_id": "18dc3669-3a95-3c2b-ab59-da3e497ba5d3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "alle honden in het algemeen"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "pejorative"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "152f2452-30bb-45da-98f5-1b4f2bd00744",
                                                "sense_id": "2135c41b-a9fb-3d89-a5d5-c57d08fef1b3",
                                                "text": "Het is 2015. Als we ergens geen behoefte meer aan hebben, dan zijn het wel paardenkoetsen. Maar in veel Europese steden zie je er nog honderden, voor de toeristen. Paarden horen lekker te rennen in een weiland of op een strand. Ze schijten bovendien alles onder. Stel je voor: hondenbezitters lopen en masse met zo’n warm boterhamzakje met de verse keutel van hun keffer in de jaszak rond om onze straten schoon te houden, terwijl paarden hun kiloknallers rustig op de tegels laten kletteren. En denk maar niet dat zo’n toeristentiller op die koets er met een zakje achteraan loopt."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "634ca0af-8ccc-31fb-8d2a-89d5917bf5d8",
                                        "entry_id": "18dc3669-3a95-3c2b-ab59-da3e497ba5d3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "iemand die een hoop misbaar maakt"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "54ab528e-7fac-467e-835e-62b8ae8bdfa0",
                                                "sense_id": "634ca0af-8ccc-31fb-8d2a-89d5917bf5d8",
                                                "text": "Een voetbaltrainer zit tijdens een wedstrijd op de bank. Of hij staat langs het veld. Heel af en toe permitteert een trainer zich iets anders, dan gaat hij achterover op het gras liggen: dat is uitzonderlijk. Ik zie graag beelden van trainers langs het veld. Ze laten zich zien als kauwgumkauwer, keffer, grappenmaker, cynicus, opnaaier, gemenerik, strateeg, idioot, notitiemaker, patiënt, publieksbespeler, vader, opa en doetje."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
